======== Leetcode 50. Pow(x, n) ======

Step-by-step algorithm to calculate x raised to the power n efficiently (using binary exponentiation):

Step 1: Convert n to a long variable N to handle negative values safely.

Step 2: Check if N is negative:

If yes, invert x → x = 1 / x

Make N positive → N = -N

Step 3: Initialize two variables:

prod = 1 → will store the final result

currp = x → will store the current power of x

Step 4: Repeat the following steps while N > 0:

Sub-step 4a: If N is odd (N % 2 == 1), multiply prod by currp.

Sub-step 4b: Square currp → currp = currp * currp.

Sub-step 4c: Divide N by 2 → N = N / 2 (integer division).

Step 5: Continue this process until N becomes 0.

Step 6: Return prod as the final result (x raised to n).

Time Complexity:

Each step halves N → O(log n)
Time Complexity = O(log n)

Space Complexity:

Only a few variables are used → O(1)


        ----------------> Code <--------------

class Solution {
    public double myPow(double x, int n) {
        long N=n;
        if(N<0){
            x=1/x;
            N=-N;
        }

        double prod=1, currp=x;
        while(N>0){
            if(N%2==1){
                prod*=currp;
            }
            currp*=currp;
            N=N/2;
        }

        return prod;
    }
}
